# xhciinst-imports.allow - every function the installer's five images
# import, by profile, architecture and module (check-imports.ps1 holds each
# image to its rows exactly: an import not listed fails, and so does a row
# the image no longer imports). A module name alone would let through a
# function only NT exports, and the 32-bit images would then not start on
# Windows 98 SE.
#
# Where the rows come from: the 3.4.1.0 release images' import tables, read
# with check-imports.ps1 -List, and the one function this tree's console
# and window images import beyond them, KERNEL32's OpenEventA (the mark
# service's idle event, design record 21 section 7.8.4), which XHCITR.EXE
# and XHCITR64.EXE of that cycle import too (xhcitr\xhcitr-imports.allow's
# x86 and amd64 rows; XHCITR.EXE started and ran on 98 SE). The
# x86 rows are the Windows 98 SE baseline: the 32-bit window, console tool
# and SETUP.EXE of that cycle started and ran on 98 SE (runs/run-46.md).
# The amd64 rows are the x64 pair's, whose ceiling is XP x64. A new x86
# row needs the function in Windows 98 SE's export table of that module
# first (a run-time lookup, GetProcAddress, needs no row); a new amd64 row
# needs it in XP x64's. COMCTL32's import library binds InitCommonControls
# by ordinal, listed as #17.
#
# profile  arch   module        function

